xnu 0250: read the UCHE trap page after the blit, page aligned

The trap probe read 16 words at offset 0xf00 of the CP's memptr page, and it
read them from the 2d-if report, which runs before run2dFill submits anything:
the one page that could show a redirected write was inspected while it was
still zero by construction. Both halves were wrong, and either one alone
would keep the answer invisible.

The trap now has a page of its own (iova 0x304000, mapped RW, WCOMB view) and
the scan runs in run2dFill after the fill's fence, over all 1024 words: a
non-zero word is a write the UCHE could not translate, which is where a
request that neither lands nor faults is expected to go.

Zero means the request never reached the UCHE. The report then reads what the
SMMU knows -- the global FSR/GFSYNR, four context banks (SCTLR, FSR, FAR,
TTBR0) and the eight low SMR/S2CR pairs -- because the port masks every
interrupt and the stream table is the other place a refused write leaves a
trace. gputrap=0 keeps mainline's 0x1fffffffff000 and skips both reads.
